  "agent_guidance": "Local reproduction (env GVM_TCK_LV=6.0.0 ./gradlew test -Pcoordinates=org.springframework:spring-aspects:5.3.31) fails native run with: com.oracle.svm.core.jdk.UnsupportedFeatureError: Classes cannot be defined at runtime ... Tried to define class: org/springframework/context/annotation/aspectj/SpringConfiguredConfiguration$$SpringCGLIB$$0. SpringConfiguredConfiguration (in spring-aspects itself) is a plain @Configuration (proxyBeanMethods=true by default) auto-imported by @EnableSpringConfigured, and Spring CGLIB-enhances it at runtime for @Bean method interception. This is the exact same class of failure already fixed for org.springframework:spring-context:6.0.0 and org.springframework:spring-aop:6.0.0 in this repo — mirror that pattern for spring-aspects: (1) add system property spring.objenesis.ignore=true to `tasks.withType(Test).configureEach`, to `nativeTest` runtimeArgs, and to `graalvmNative.binaries.test.buildArgs`; (2) add a `generatePredefinedCglibProxyClasses` JavaExec task (see PredefinedCglibProxyClassesGenerator.java under tests/src/org.springframework/spring-context/6.0.0/src/test/java and tests/src/org.springframework/spring-aop/6.0.0/src/test/java) that forks a JVM with `-Dcglib.debugLocation=<compiled test classes dir>` and `-Dspring.objenesis.ignore=true`, exercises the code path that triggers the CGLIB enhancement (e.g. instantiate the @EnableSpringConfigured config, as in the existing springConfiguredRegistersTheSingletonBeanConfigurerAspect test) so SpringConfiguredConfiguration$$SpringCGLIB$$0.class is dumped onto the compiled test-classes directory, then verify that expected class file exists; (3) make `nativeTestCompile` and `nativeTraceImage` depend on that task. Do not add the `org.glassfish:javax.ejb:3.1` dependency used in spring-context/6.0.0 — that's unrelated to this fix. If future test coverage adds @EnableCaching/@EnableTransactionManagement/@EnableAsync with the default AdviceMode.PROXY (the current test only uses AdviceMode.ASPECTJ, which doesn't need CGLIB), those would need their own proxy classes added to the same predefinition generator.",
